    "expectedRule": "Combat Replay Stage freezes entry gear {frameEngraver, cueVisor, bufferPlate, thawMetronome} from the equipped loadout into law.entryGear at dungeon entry (weapon frame_engraver, head cue_visor, armor buffer_plate, charm thaw_metronome). Three take nodes (take_alpha, take_beta, take_gamma) each record the first direct combat action fought there: attack/art/guard records a take {action, observedValue, replayValue} where observedValue is the real combat event value (actual damage dealt to the monster for attack/art, pure guard reduction for guard) and replayValue = frameEngraver ? min(9999, ceil(observedValue * 1.15)) : observedValue. Takes must be recorded in order alpha→beta→gamma: take-entry gates close take_beta/take_gamma until the earlier takes are recorded ('先完成第 1 段母带，再进入第 2 段录制。') and take-exit gates block leaving a take node until its take is recorded ('录制当前战斗母带后才能离开。'; the move itself is departure-blocked by the uncleared monster). The law display is `1:攻击 X->Y，2:战技 Z->W，3:防御 U->V，路线:未选择，Boss快照:未冻结` with severity danger/warning/stable/resolved and meter {value: completedTakeCount, max: 3}. After three takes, law/select-combat-replay-route {route} permanently selects one of sequence/burst/afterbeat (log 复演路线已冻结：顺序剪辑。); a second selection is a domain-rejected no-op. Route nodes carry selection gates: only the selected route's node opens ('三段母带完成后选择顺序路线；其余路线将永久关闭。' etc.), the others stay closed and run/move through them is rejected illegal-move. The boss gate to final_cut_director is a composite all-conditions gate ('需同时满足这条战痕复演门的全部条件。') that opens only with three takes plus a selected route ('完成三段母带并选择复演路线后，最终剪辑师入口开放。'); moving onto the boss before that is illegal-move. Starting the final_cut_director boss combat freezes bossSnapshot {takes, route} and makes the law immutable: the route can no longer be re-selected (domain-rejected). With thaw_metronome equipped, the boss opening releases take_alpha's replay at 75% route percent plus the cue_visor first-boost (+25%, once per combat) — for the sequence route that is 100% of replayValue 248 = 248 fixed damage (log take_alpha复演「攻」，造成 248 点固定伤害。). During the boss fight a sealed-phase direct action matching the cursor's recorded take releases its replayValue at the sequence route's 100% (take_beta art → 271 fixed damage) and advances the cursor; the boss awakens (删镜杀青) mid-fight, and in the awakened phase matching actions no longer release, so the take_gamma guard replay never fires in this band — the frozen cursor/buffer after the guard turn is the dynamic equivalent evidence that awakened matching actions do not release. In normal (non-boss) combats after a route is selected, the recorded takes replay as fixed damage/buffer at the route percent: sequence releases the cursor take at 100% before each direct action (cue_visor first-boost makes the first release 125% → replayValue 248 → 310 fixed damage); burst releases all three takes at 60% at the combat opening (248→210 with the first-boost, 271→162, guard 3→1 buffer) and the buffer_plate makes the guard buffer absorb two counter-hits (复演缓冲抵消 1 点反击伤害，剩余承伤次数 1。). Route percents are sequence 100, burst 60, afterbeat 125. Node rewards are idempotent: collecting stage_gate pays once (rewardPoints 850→1430, run loot 580, focus_incense/dispel_talisman/armor_patch 3→4, gate_sigil 1) and a second collect is domain-rejected ('复演场正门已经领取过奖励。'). Law state (takes, route, bossSnapshot, entryGear), display status, and reward points persist through a save-codec round-trip. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
